exit 2
--- stdout ---

The GitHub CLI (gh) is not installed, so bbapprove cannot download the release for you. Manually:
  1. open https://github.com/example/repo/releases/latest and note the tag (<tag>)
  2. download bbapprove-<tag>-linux-amd64.tar.gz and SHA256SUMS from that release page into an empty directory
  3. verify:  shasum -a 256 -c SHA256SUMS --ignore-missing
  4. extract: tar -xzf bbapprove-<tag>-linux-amd64.tar.gz   (creates a new directory; do not unpack over the current install $BASE/bbapprove-v1.0.0-rc.2-linux-amd64)
  5. switch by re-pointing your bbapprove symlink to <new>/bin/bbapprove; keep the old tree for rollback
Or install gh (https://cli.github.com), run `gh auth login` and re-run bbapprove --update.
